(:id "go/R16" :state :unknown :note "the title's last clause, \"copy/const/present/ordinal move nothing\", is not held on the go leg: §5.4 puts the forged ordinal's clamped in the BOUNDS pass on both plans and says a port that counts in the op as well counts twice, and fix 27 says a leg that counts it in the op has the op to move; this leg counts it in tableFixedOrdinal (the compiled plan) and tableFixedConst (the identity plan) — schema#1254, §5.8 row 12. The numeric clauses (widened once per entry per record, a folded element run is ONE, the compile census once per peer) need a running load over the reference corpus, which this card cannot build. The census-once-per-peer and widen-site structure this leg does hold are asserted in internal/codegen/gotable/fixedroadmap_t04_test.go:TestFixedRoadmapGoT04VersionsEvolution/go/R16.")
